using DroidSpeak;
using DroidSpeak.DSP;

namespace DroidSpeak.Tests;

/// <summary>
/// Golden PCM snapshots captured from v0.3.0 before the v0.4.0 prosody/DSP split and re-signed for
/// the v0.5 expressive layer.
/// <para>
/// The goldens are <see cref="PcmFingerprint"/> acoustic signatures instead of raw float SHA-256
/// digests. The platform math libraries (<c>ucrtbase</c>, <c>glibc</c>, <c>libm</c>) disagree by a
/// unit in the last place and the oscillator and filter state integrates that difference, so byte
/// hashing only ever agreed on the machine that produced the golden — which is why the snapshot
/// suite failed wholesale on Linux CI while passing locally on Windows. Timing is still compared
/// exactly, and the energy, spectral and envelope metrics are compared within tight tolerances, so
/// a real DSP change still trips these snapshots on every platform.
/// </para>
/// </summary>
public class PcmSnapshotTests
{
